    "body": "## Motivation\n\nFlux2 packs Q, K, and V in one projection and then `chunk`s them. Those K/V tensors are views, so they are not contiguous. With `--num-gpus 2` and sequence parallel left on its default, SGLang selects `kv_gather_degree=2`. The full-sequence gather then calls `all_gather_into_tensor` on that view. PyTorch's NCCL process group (`check_gpu_single_tensor`) rejects it with `ValueError: Tensors must be contiguous` before the collective runs. The same check is in the CUDA build, so NVIDIA hits it on this path too. The prefix and suffix branches already called `.contiguous()`. The unsliced branch did not, and that is the branch Flux2 takes.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `USPAttention._gather_sharded_sequence` materializes the unsliced K/V tensor with `.contiguous()` before `sequence_model_parallel_all_gather`.\n- `GroupCoordinator.all_gather` does the same immediately before `all_gather_into_tensor`, so any other non-contiguous caller of that collective meets the NCCL/RCCL requirement. An already-contiguous tensor is returned unchanged.\n- `test/registered/unit/layers/attention/test_sp_kv_gather_contiguous.py` builds a K tensor with `chunk`, asserts it is not contiguous, and asserts the tensor passed into the gather is contiguous and equal to the original view. CPU CI: `base-a-test-cpu`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nSame prompt, seed 42, 720p, 50 steps, `torch.compile` on. The 1-GPU image is `20261012-055625`. The 2-GPU kv-gather image after this fix is `20261012-071319`. Both are 1280x720. The broken run saved no image, so this is 1-GPU versus 2-GPU sequence parallel, not a before/after of the copy. The unit test checks that `.contiguous()` keeps the same values as the view.\n\n| metric | value |\n| --- | --- |\n| mean abs (0-255) | 2.46 |\n| RMSE | 8.42 |\n| max abs | 255 |\n| PSNR | 29.6 dB |\n| pixels with abs diff > 8 | 8.6% |\n\n## Benchmarking and Profiling\n\nMI355, Flux2-dev, 720p, 50 steps, seed 42, `torch.compile` on. The 2-GPU kv-gather run aborted before the fix, so it has no latency.\n\n| config | result | denoising | per step |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 GPU | completed | 24.79 s | 0.409 s |\n| 2 GPU kv-gather, before | abort: `Tensors must be contiguous` | — | — |\n| 2 GPU kv-gather, after | image saved | 20.19 s | 0.351 s |\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the PR flow. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`, `/tag-and-rerun-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls to merge.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38218178187](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38218178187)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38218177890](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38218177890)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38218178105](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38218178105)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
